<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_aid_flow" target="comms_cyber_warfare::compute_infra_utilizatio" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Large, rapid deliveries of ISR, ISR-processing kits, and networked sensors included in military aid create immediate demand for image/telemetry processing and cloud/edge AI, raising utilization of existing compute infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">comms_cyber_warfare</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_aid_flow" target="comms_cyber_warfare::ai_agent_prevalence" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Military aid packages increasingly include autonomous systems (loitering munitions, autonomous ISR drones, autonomy-enabled munitions), directly increasing the deployed stock of autonomous AI agents in the operational battlespace.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">comms_cyber_warfare</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_aid_flow" target="global_oil_rebalance::chokepoint_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased deliveries of long‑range and anti‑ship weaponry to frontline actors raise the likelihood of strikes, mines, and defensive countermeasures in and around maritime approaches, producing more interruptions and delays at regional chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_rebalance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_aid_flow" target="iran_gulf_escalation::naval_deployment_lvl" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A surge in military aid to Ukraine prompts US/NATO to reassign surface combatants, escorts and logistical support from the Persian Gulf toward European seas and Atlantic/Mediterranean staging, directly reducing aggregate naval presence in the Gulf theatre.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
