  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Large committed government contracts and reconstruction/defense funding raise expected future revenues for defense-tech and AI suppliers, which fuels investor speculation and upward re-rating of related technology and AI assets.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">comms_cyber_warfare</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::funding_commitment_stock" target="global_oil_rebalance::market_supply_expect" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Large new or expanded committed funding signals to traders that the conflict and associated export disruptions are likely to be prolonged, shifting aggregated expectations toward tighter future crude availability.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_rebalance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::funding_commitment_stock" target="iran_gulf_escalation::shipping_insurance_idx" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Large, sustained funding commitments for Ukraine increase fiscal pressure and risk‑appetite constraints among Western backers, prompting insurers to price a higher premium on Gulf routes because underwriters anticipate thinner security guarantees and greater operational risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::funding_commitment_stock" target="transatlantic_cohesion::bond_yield_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising cumulative commitments to military aid and reconstruction raise expected sovereign borrowing needs and the term premium, putting upward pressure on long‑term government yields as markets anticipate larger issuance.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">transatlantic_cohesion</data>
</edge>
