<edge source="global_oil_rebalance::crude_futures_price" target="comms_cyber_warfare::valuation_exuberance" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in crude futures lifts expectations for energy and logistics costs, compressing forward cash‑flow multiples for high‑burn tech/AI firms and triggering de‑risking and de‑rating in valuation‑driven segments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_rebalance</data>
  <data key="d39">comms_cyber_warfare</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_rebalance::crude_futures_price" target="iran_gulf_escalation::maritime_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained higher futures prices raise the value of successful supply shocks and increase net revenue available to state and proxy actors, incentivizing more maritime harassment and attacks to extract concessions or influence market flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_rebalance</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_rebalance::crude_futures_price" target="russia_ukraine_war::funding_commitment_stock" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained elevated crude futures prices raise domestic energy costs and fiscal pressures in donor countries, increasing political resistance to new large budgetary commitments and thus slowing or shrinking formal funding pledges for the Ukraine effort.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_rebalance</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_rebalance::crude_futures_price" target="transatlantic_cohesion::cb_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in traded crude futures visibly raises near‑term headline inflation risks in transatlantic economies, prompting markets to price a higher probability of earlier and larger central‑bank tightening.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_rebalance</data>
  <data key="d39">transatlantic_cohesion</data>
</edge>
