<edge source="transatlantic_cohesion::capital_flow_volatility" target="comms_cyber_warfare::systemic_coupling" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in cross‑border capital‑flow volatility force rapid balance‑sheet adjustments and reliance on common liquidity providers and contracts, immediately strengthening interdependencies across markets and infrastructure nodes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">transatlantic_cohesion</data>
  <data key="d39">comms_cyber_warfare</data>
</edge>
<edge source="transatlantic_cohesion::capital_flow_volatility" target="global_oil_rebalance::market_supply_expect" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher capital‑flow volatility tightens external and project financing conditions for marginal oil producers and service firms, lowering market expectations of future crude supply availability.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">transatlantic_cohesion</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_rebalance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="transatlantic_cohesion::capital_flow_volatility" target="iran_gulf_escalation::shipping_insurance_idx" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in cross‑border capital‑flow volatility tighten reinsurer/investor capacity and raise risk premia for underwriting, leading insurers to impose higher premiums and surcharges on vessels operating in the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">transatlantic_cohesion</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="transatlantic_cohesion::capital_flow_volatility" target="russia_ukraine_war::interparty_trust_level" id="0">
