  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in capital-flow volatility force some allies to prioritize domestic financial stability and can produce abrupt funding or procurement reversals, which allied partners interpret as unreliable behaviour and erode mutual trust.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">transatlantic_cohesion</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
